Subject: [PATCH] docs: document the MCP server in the root README

Glama's indexer reads the repository root README to confirm a submission
implements an MCP server. The root README only covered the oracle API and the
TypeScript SDK, so the hosannaith-mcp server (which lives in mcp/) wasn't
visible there and the Glama submission was rejected as "not an MCP server".

Add a "Use it from any MCP agent" section covering the MCP server, its three
MCP tools, the @modelcontextprotocol/sdk it is built on, the npm package, and
the official MCP Registry listing (io.github.cameron4316/hosannaith-mcp).

